  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing the Humanitarian, Protection and Health Needs of Undocumented Returnees at the Borders and Longer-Term Needs of Returnees and Internally Displaces Persons (IDPs) in Key Provinces of High Return</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan is facing an unprecedented humanitarian crisis with a very real risk of systemic collapse and human catastrophe. In addition to unimaginable human costs, this humanitarian crisis is reversing many of the gains of the last 20 years, including around women&#x2019;s rights. The objective of this 12-month project is to ensure the continuity of humanitarian assistance provided to vulnerable undocumented returnees at the border, addressing the longer-term needs of returnees and internally displaced persons (IDPs) in key provinces of high return through improved access to livelihoods.</narrative>
  </description>
